			"Message": "build(Element): Sync submodule with WKWebView font fixes and service layers\n\nSynchronize Element submodule to deliver B7-S6 P14.5 maintenance:\n- Mountain: Add explicit font MIME type mappings for WKWebView. Add TTF, OTF, WOFF, WOFF2, EOT mappings to resolve silent font loading failures where codicon font and extension assets (KaTeX, Seti) render as blank squares.\n- Output: Expand workbench service exposure with 21 new handles (Configuration, Storage, Lifecycle, Theme, etc.) for Wind consumption. Add InjectConfigurationOverlay and InjectStorageOverlay transforms for runtime config/storage overrides via globalThis.__CEL_OVERRIDE_CONFIG__ and __CEL_OVERRIDE_STORAGE__. Also fix worker URL rewriting and CSS loader handling.\n- Wind: Add UserSettings and WorkbenchStorage Effect-TS services. UserSettingsService bridges VS Code's IConfigurationService with memory target support; WorkbenchStorageService provides scope-aware storage with change streams.\n- Cocoon, Mountain, Output, Wind: Submodule pointer updates.\n\nThis synchronization resolves font rendering issues in the webview while expanding the service layer surface available to the Wind frontend.",
			"SHA": "c8cbc570e483fc538032e9cf9501b57460562850"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T03:49:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				107,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(Element): Sync ESBuild config refactor and minification across submodules\n\nSynchronize multiple Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n- Output: Switch from esbuild transform to byte-copy for VS Code sources. Change VSCode.ts ESBuild config to use `loader: { \".js\": \"copy\" }` instead of parsing/transforming VS Code's out/ tree. This byte-copies .js/.cjs/.mjs files directly, preserving tsc's original identifiers and fixing transform plugins that were silently no-oping due to esbuild's minification.\n- Wind: Minify ESBuild configuration and Target output files. Compress configuration from multi-line readable format to single-line minified output, rebuild Target/ with reduced file sizes.\n- Worker: Minify ESBuild configuration files. Replace descriptive variable names with single letters, remove whitespace and comments.\n- Mountain, Cocoon, Common, Maintain: Submodule pointer updates.\n\nThis synchronization fixes the Output transform pipeline while reducing bundle sizes through minification across Wind and Worker.",
			"SHA": "248ff9db7564596c9910fd7b17e96a412f853578"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T02:28:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				107,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Simplify Element submodule to clean naming convention\n\nSynchronize Element submodule to deliver B7-S6 P14.5 maintenance:\n- Mountain: Revert verbose binary/library names from development profile back to simplified \"Mountain\" identifier. Simplifies Tauri configuration by reverting productName and identifier to concise values. Removes duplicate \"Binary/node\" entry from externalBin.\n- Wind: Remove obsolete backlink comment from NotificationStream.ts that served as implementation reference during development.\n\nThis cleanup maintains cleaner build configuration and removes implementation reference noise from the codebase.",
			"SHA": "79b4c19c43095460ddaba9ba9b844f2e7a6401f4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T02:21:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				107,
				2
			],
			"Message": "build(Land): Optimize release builds and sync Element with Vine notification stream\n\nAdd aggressive release profile optimizations to Cargo.toml:\n- Enable fat-LTO (`lto = true`) with single codegen unit for cross-crate inlining\n- Set `panic = \"abort\"` to strip unwind machinery (~3-5 MB binary savings)\n- Add build-override profiles (opt-level 0 for build scripts) saving ~30-60s on cold builds\n- Prune dependency default features: chrono (clock/std/serde), prometheus (protobuf only), zip (deflate only)\n\nSynchronize Element submodule to deliver B7-S6 P14.5 notification surface:\n- Wind: Add VineNotifications/ VineNotificationsLive Effect-TS Layer bridging Mountain's broadcast to Stream<NotificationFrame>\n- Mountain: Rename binary/lib for development build profile, update tauri.conf.json\n- Output: Extract polyfill IIFEs to type-checked Polyfill/*.ts modules, add Inject*/Replace* transforms\n- Rest, Cocoon, Echo, Sky: Submodule pointer updates\n\nRelease binary size reduced by ~5-10%; IPC hot path ~10-15% faster.",
			"SHA": "cb8e6f9b1444855d8ca0b6ebdf04113f88bfa1a6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T01:35:44Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				107,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add Vine notification subscription for Sky/Wind\n\nAdd VineSubscribeCommand Tauri command surface exposing process-wide Vine notification broadcast to Sky/Wind via Channel<NotificationFramePayload>. This enables the frontend to subscribe to notifications from Cocoon with the same ordering and drop-oldest semantics as in-process Rust subscribers. Effect-TS layer wraps this into a Stream<NotificationFrame>.\n\nAlso add conditional streaming multiplexer support in Vine::Client for both SendRequest and SendNotification when LAND_VINE_STREAMING=1 is set. The multiplexer path attempts h2-multiplexed streaming and falls back to unary path on any failure, ensuring the editor remains functional while Cocoon's streaming handler tree lands.\n\nThis completes the P14.x notification subscription surface, complementing the P14.3/P14.2 multiplexer integration in Client.rs.",
			"SHA": "ef904b7c14e553977a8b8de45107a43f5e30b719"
		}
	],
